<!--meta {"lead": "Links take people somewhere: to a style, a braider's profile, the terms. They are always underlined, so they never rely on colour alone.", "description": "Inline, standalone with arrow and external links, with hover, focus and active states in both themes.", "pills": ["Native <code>&lt;a href&gt;</code>", "Status: stable"], "variants": "inline, standalone with arrow, external, inherit (in alerts and footers)", "states": "default, hover, focus, active", "sources": ["pages/style-gallery/default", "pages/braider-profile/default", "pages/terms/default", "pages/style-detail/partial"]} -->
<section class="ds-section" id="overview"><h2><a href="#overview">Overview</a></h2>
  <p>Use a link when activating it navigates: to another page, a section, a route-backed dialog, or an external site. Use a <a href="button.html">button</a> when activating it changes something. A button-styled link (<code>&lt;a class="btn"&gt;</code>) is still a link and follows these rules for its markup.</p>
  <ul>
    <li><b>Inline</b> links sit inside running text: "Read <a href="#overview">Nia’s cancellation policy</a> before you send a request."</li>
    <li><b>Standalone</b> links end a card or section and carry an arrow: "Explore Knotless braids". One per card.</li>
    <li><b>External</b> links leave HairPop. They show the external icon and say "opens in a new tab" when they do.</li>
    <li><b>Inherit</b> links take the colour of their container in alerts, toasts, breadcrumbs and the footer, and stay underlined.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="anatomy"><h2><a href="#anatomy">Anatomy</a></h2>
  <div class="ds-anatomy">
    <figure class="ds-anatomy__figure">
      <a class="link link--standalone" href="../../mocks/pages/style-detail/default.html">Explore Knotless braids <span class="link__arrow" aria-hidden="true">{{icon:arrow-right|icon--sm}}</span></a>
      <span class="ds-callout" style="left: 30%; top: 26%;" aria-hidden="true">1</span>
      <span class="ds-callout" style="left: 46%; top: 72%;" aria-hidden="true">2</span>
      <span class="ds-callout" style="left: 69%; top: 26%;" aria-hidden="true">3</span>
    </figure>
    <ol class="ds-anatomy__list">
      <li><div><b>Text</b><small>Says where the link goes; it is the accessible name.</small></div></li>
      <li><div><b>Underline</b><small>1px at rest, 2px on hover, 0.15em offset. Never removed.</small></div></li>
      <li><div><b>Trailing icon (optional)</b><small>Arrow for standalone links, external icon for other sites; <code>aria-hidden</code>.</small></div></li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="variants"><h2><a href="#variants">Variants</a></h2>
  {{example:[stack,start]Inline, standalone and external links; all underlined.}}
<p>Read <a class="link" href="../../mocks/pages/terms/default.html">HairPop’s terms of use</a> before you send your first request.</p>
<a class="link link--standalone" href="../../mocks/pages/style-detail/default.html">Explore Knotless braids <span class="link__arrow" aria-hidden="true">{{icon:arrow-right|icon--sm}}</span></a>
<p>Read the <a class="link link--external" href="https://www.w3.org/WAI/standards-guidelines/wcag/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">WCAG 2.2 guidelines{{icon:external|icon--sm}}<span class="visually-hidden"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a> before you start.</p>
  {{/example}}
  <h3>Inherit colour</h3>
  <p><code>.link--inherit</code> takes the container's text colour and stays underlined, so it keeps the container's contrast pair and still reads as a link. Containers tune it with two knobs rather than reaching into the link: <code>--link-inherit-font-weight</code> (alerts and the error summary set it to semibold) and <code>--link-inherit-hover-fg</code> (the footer sets it to <code>--color-fg-default</code>). With neither set, the link keeps the container's weight and colour on hover too, and only the underline thickens.</p>
  {{example:[stack]The partial-load alert on Nia’s profile with a retry link, and the footer links.}}
<div><div class="alert alert--warning">{{icon:warning}}<div class="alert__body"><p class="alert__title">Some details are unavailable</p><p>Reviews could not load.</p><div class="alert__actions"><a class="link link--inherit" href="../../mocks/pages/braider-profile/default.html">Retry reviews</a></div></div></div></div>
<footer class="site-footer"><span>HairPop · Made for confident hair decisions</span><span><a class="link link--inherit" href="../../mocks/pages/terms/default.html">Terms</a> · <a class="link link--inherit" href="../../mocks/pages/privacy/default.html">Privacy</a></span></footer>
  {{/example}}
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="sizes" data-na="Links take the size of the text they sit in; standalone links use the label font at 16px."><h2><a href="#sizes">Sizes</a></h2></section>

<section class="ds-section" id="states"><h2><a href="#states">States</a></h2>
  <p>Hover thickens the underline and darkens the colour; focus shows the shared ring; active keeps the hover colour. Visited links are not restyled: HairPop's links mostly lead back to the same browsing pages, so a visited colour would add noise rather than orientation. Links have no disabled state; remove the link instead.</p>
  <div class="ds-matrix"><table>
    <thead><tr><th scope="col">Variant</th><th scope="col">Default</th><th scope="col">Hover</th><th scope="col">Focus</th><th scope="col">Active</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><th scope="row">Inline</th><td><a class="link" href="#states">Nia’s policy</a></td><td><a class="link" href="#states" data-state="hover">Nia’s policy</a></td><td><a class="link" href="#states" data-state="focus">Nia’s policy</a></td><td><a class="link" href="#states" data-state="active">Nia’s policy</a></td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">Standalone</th><td><a class="link link--standalone" href="#states">Explore Cornrows <span class="link__arrow" aria-hidden="true">{{icon:arrow-right|icon--sm}}</span></a></td><td><a class="link link--standalone" href="#states" data-state="hover">Explore Cornrows <span class="link__arrow" aria-hidden="true">{{icon:arrow-right|icon--sm}}</span></a></td><td><a class="link link--standalone" href="#states" data-state="focus">Explore Cornrows <span class="link__arrow" aria-hidden="true">{{icon:arrow-right|icon--sm}}</span></a></td><td><a class="link link--standalone" href="#states" data-state="active">Explore Cornrows <span class="link__arrow" aria-hidden="true">{{icon:arrow-right|icon--sm}}</span></a></td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table></div>
  <h3>Both themes</h3>
  {{themes:stack}}<p>Read <a class="link" href="#states">Nia’s cancellation policy</a> first.</p><a class="link link--standalone" href="#states">Explore Passion twists <span class="link__arrow" aria-hidden="true">{{icon:arrow-right|icon--sm}}</span></a>{{/themes}}
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="responsive"><h2><a href="#responsive">Responsive behaviour</a></h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Inline links wrap with their sentence; never set <code>white-space: nowrap</code> on long link text.</li>
    <li>Standalone links are at least 24px tall (<code>--target-min</code>) so they meet the target size on phones; give them their own line in cards. When the label wraps (narrow cards, 200% text) the arrow keeps its 1rem size at the end of the row (<code>.link__arrow</code> is <code>flex: none</code>).</li>
    <li>The external icon sits on the text line after the last word and wraps with it (<code>display: inline-block</code>, <code>vertical-align: -0.125em</code>).</li>
    <li>Footer links keep 24px targets and wrap onto a second line below 640px.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="theming"><h2><a href="#theming">Theming</a></h2>
  <p>Links read <code>--color-fg-link</code> and <code>--color-fg-link-hover</code>. In light they are plum 700 and 800; in dark plum 300 and 200, all above 7:1 on every surface. Inside alerts, toasts, breadcrumbs and the footer the link inherits (<code>.link--inherit</code>, <code>color: inherit</code>) so it never introduces a new contrast pair; containers set <code>--link-inherit-font-weight</code> and <code>--link-inherit-hover-fg</code> to re-skin it.</p>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="accessibility"><h2><a href="#accessibility">Accessibility</a></h2>
  <h3>Role and pattern</h3>
  <p>Native <code>&lt;a href&gt;</code>; see the <a href="https://www.w3.org/WAI/ARIA/apg/patterns/link/">APG Link pattern</a>. Never an anchor without <code>href</code>, never a <code>&lt;span&gt;</code> with a click handler.</p>
  <h3>Keyboard</h3>
  <table class="ds-table ds-keys"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Key</th><th scope="col">Action</th></tr></thead><tbody>
    <tr><td><kbd>Tab</kbd> / <kbd>Shift</kbd>+<kbd>Tab</kbd></td><td>Moves focus between links in DOM order.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><kbd>Enter</kbd></td><td>Follows the link. (<kbd>Space</kbd> scrolls the page; it does not follow links.)</td></tr>
  </tbody></table>
  <h3>Focus</h3>
  <p>The shared 2px ring with 2px offset on <code>:focus-visible</code>. Standalone links are inline-flex, so the ring wraps the text and arrow as one shape.</p>
  <h3>Labelling</h3>
  <p>Link text makes sense alone (SC 2.4.4): "Explore Knotless braids", not "Explore" or "Learn more". Repeated card links name their card. Decorative arrows are <code>aria-hidden</code>; external links add a visually hidden "(opens in a new tab)" when they use <code>target="_blank"</code>.</p>
  <h3>Contrast</h3>
  <div class="ds-example__canvas ds-example__canvas--stack" style="padding: 0; gap: var(--space-2);">
    {{pair:Link on page|--color-fg-link|--color-bg-canvas|4.5}}
    {{pair:Link on card|--color-fg-link|--color-bg-surface|4.5}}
    {{pair:Hovered link on card|--color-fg-link-hover|--color-bg-surface|4.5}}
  </div>
  <p>The underline, not colour, distinguishes links from text (SC 1.4.1).</p>
  <h3>Motion</h3>
  <p>The standalone arrow shifts 4px right on hover over <code>--duration-fast</code>; reduced motion makes it instant.</p>
  <h3>Touch</h3>
  <p>Standalone and footer links are at least 24px tall. Inline links inside paragraphs fall under the SC 2.5.8 inline exception but are never placed closer than one word apart.</p>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="content"><h2><a href="#content">Content</a></h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Describe the destination: "Explore Knotless braids", "Read Nia’s reviews", "Terms of use".</li>
    <li>Use sentence case and no trailing punctuation inside the link.</li>
    <li>Do not start with "Click here" or "Link to"; screen readers already announce "link".</li>
    <li>Keep the arrow for standalone links only; inline links never carry icons except the external icon.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="do-dont"><h2><a href="#do-dont">Do and don't</a></h2>
  <div class="ds-dodont">
    <figure class="ds-do"><div class="ds-example__canvas"><a class="link link--standalone" href="#do-dont">Explore Knotless braids <span class="link__arrow" aria-hidden="true">{{icon:arrow-right|icon--sm}}</span></a></div><figcaption>Name the card in the link and draw the arrow as an icon.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="ds-dont"><div class="ds-example__canvas"><a href="#do-dont">Explore Knotless braids <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div><figcaption>Draw the arrow as a "→" text glyph with no minimum target height, as the first gallery mock did.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="ds-do"><div class="ds-example__canvas"><a class="link" href="../../mocks/dialogs/report-review/default.html">Report a review</a></div><figcaption>Use a link to open a route-backed dialog such as "Report a review".</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="ds-dont"><div class="ds-example__canvas"><button class="btn btn--link" type="button">Terms</button></div><figcaption>A button styled as a link for navigation: it cannot open in a new tab and announces the wrong role.</figcaption></figure>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="tokens"><h2><a href="#tokens">Tokens</a></h2>
  <div class="ds-table-wrap"><table class="ds-table">
    <thead><tr><th scope="col">Part</th><th scope="col">Token</th><th scope="col">Light</th><th scope="col">Dark</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      {{tok:Text|--color-fg-link}}
      {{tok:Text, hover and active|--color-fg-link-hover}}
      {{tok:Focus ring|--color-focus-ring}}
      {{tok:Underline width rest / hover|--border-width-hairline|--border-width-thick}}
      {{tok:Standalone label font|--text-label}}
      {{tok:Standalone min height|--target-min}}
      {{tok:Arrow shift|--space-1|--duration-fast}}
    </tbody>
  </table></div>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="code"><h2><a href="#code">Code</a></h2>
  <pre><code>&lt;p&gt;Read &lt;a class="link" href="/terms"&gt;HairPop’s terms of use&lt;/a&gt; first.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;a class="link link--standalone" href="/styles/knotless-braids"&gt;
  Explore Knotless braids
  &lt;span class="link__arrow" aria-hidden="true"&gt;&lt;svg class="icon icon--sm" …&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/a&gt;

&lt;a class="link link--external" href="https://example.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener"&gt;
  Partner site&lt;svg class="icon icon--sm" aria-hidden="true" …&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;
  &lt;span class="visually-hidden"&gt; (opens in a new tab)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/a&gt;</code></pre>
  <table class="ds-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Class / attribute</th><th scope="col">Effect</th></tr></thead><tbody>
    <tr><td><code>.link</code> (and bare <code>a[href]</code> in rich text)</td><td>Inline link: link colour, 1px underline, 2px on hover and active.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>.link--standalone</code></td><td>Label font, 24px minimum height, icon gap.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>.link__arrow</code></td><td>Arrow wrapper that shifts right on hover and never shrinks.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>.link--external</code></td><td>External icon on the text line; opens in a new tab.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>.link--inherit</code></td><td>Container colour, underlined; reads <code>--link-inherit-font-weight</code> and <code>--link-inherit-hover-fg</code>.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>target="_blank" rel="noopener"</code></td><td>External only, with the external icon and hidden "(opens in a new tab)".</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>data-state="hover|focus|active"</code></td><td>Documentation only.</td></tr>
  </tbody></table>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="sources"><h2><a href="#sources">Sources</a></h2>
  <p>Extracted from these mocks:</p>
  <ul>
    {{mock:pages/style-gallery/default|standalone "Explore …" links on story cards, footer links}}
    {{mock:pages/braider-profile/default|"Report a review" link}}
    {{mock:pages/style-detail/partial|"Retry reviews" link inside a warning alert}}
    {{mock:pages/terms/default|footer links on long-form pages}}
  </ul>
  <p>Drift fixed during extraction: the arrow was a "→" text glyph (now the arrow icon in <code>.link__arrow</code>); standalone links had no minimum height (now 24px); footer links were under 24px tall (now 24px).</p>
</section>
